{
"opening": "This release, version 2.9.1, focuses on stabilizing the command-line interface and introducing validation capabilities for semantic versions. It addresses critical bugs in argument handling and adds new functionality to verify version string validity. These changes ensure robust behavior for both programmatic usage and CLI interactions.",
"requirements": [
{
"id": "m07",
"text": "When the pysemver command is invoked without arguments, it must raise a SystemExit error rather than crashing with an AttributeError. When the bump subcommand is called without specific arguments, it must print the help text for that subcommand and exit gracefully."
},
{
"id": "m12",
"text": "The internal regex used for parsing version strings must be updated to align with the official semver.org specification. This update ensures that invalid Python 2.7 super calls are resolved while maintaining compatibility with standard version formats."
},
{
"id": "m17",
"text": "The VersionInfo class must expose a static method named isvalid that accepts a version string and returns a boolean indicating whether the string conforms to the semantic versioning format. The pysemver CLI must include a check subcommand that utilizes this validation logic."
},
{
"id": "m19",
"text": "The public API must expose cmd_bump, cmd_check, and cmd_compare functions as distinct entry points for their respective subcommands. The createparser, finalize_version, and process functions must continue to operate correctly with these refactored subcommand handlers."
}
],
"closing": "Please ensure all public names listed above are accessible and behave as described. The documentation should reflect these updates, particularly regarding the new validation features and CLI improvements."
}
